<section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00004"><exercise id="_741e766d-8bc5-47dd-9de6-745f6ed37a69" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00017"><para id="para-00062">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00063"> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00017"><para id="para-00064">Correct! \(2(-3)^2=2 \cdot 9=18\)</para><para id="para-00065">The correct answer is 18. \(2(-3)^2=2 \cdot 9=18\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="f6d75941-6000-4943-a2bb-c1fa0c310e0b" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00018"><para id="para-00066">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00067"> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00018"><para id="para-00068">Correct! \(2(-2)^2=2 \cdot 4=8\)</para><para id="para-00069">The correct answer is 8. \(2(-2)^2=2 \cdot 4=8\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_7a7b18dd-3cf5-4867-af32-5236de55f86d" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00019"><para id="para-00070">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00071"> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00019"><para id="para-00072">Correct! \(2(-1)2=2 \cdot 1=2\)</para><para id="para-00073">The correct answer is 2. \(2(-1)2=2 \cdot 1=2\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="ed8cb8ce-10ca-4b3c-8733-b9355270955f" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00020"><para id="para-00074">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00075"> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00020"><para id="para-00076">Correct! \(2(0)^2=2 \cdot 0=0\)</para><para id="para-00077">The correct answer is 0. \(2(0)^2=2 \cdot 0=0\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_16af383e-a948-4a67-90c8-6921a04c6dc4" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00021"><para id="para-00078">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00079"> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00021"><para id="para-00080">Correct! \(2(1)^2=2 \cdot 1=2\)</para><para id="para-00081">The correct answer is 2. \(2(1)^2=2 \cdot 1=2\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_55dbbb41-7edf-4c57-8ee1-18495cce6d54" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00022"><para id="para-00082">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00083"> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00022"><para id="para-00084">Correct! \(2(2)^2=2 \cdot 4=8\)</para><para id="para-00085">The correct answer is 8. \(2(2)^2=2 \cdot 4=8\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_6a173281-6359-4277-9e56-378b2c27cddd" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00023"><para id="para-00086">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00087"> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00023"><para id="para-00088">Correct! \(2(3)^2=2 \cdot 9=18\)</para><para id="para-00089">The correct answer is 18. \(2(3)^2=2 \cdot 9=18\)</para></solution></exercise></section>
