<section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00005"><exercise id="_12964d60-9f81-4912-977d-ded91307039c" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00024"><para id="para-00090">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00091"> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00024"><para id="para-00092">Correct! \(\frac{1}{2}(-3)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 9=\frac{9}{2}=4\frac{1}{2}=4.5\)</para><para id="para-00093">The correct answer is 4.5. \(\frac{1}{2}(-3)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 9=\frac{9}{2}=4\frac{1}{2}=4.5\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="e3e9bc8c-3d92-4254-833a-c959d25c753d" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00025"><para id="para-00094">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00095"> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00025"><para id="para-00096">Correct! \(\frac{1}{2}(-2)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 4=\frac{4}{2}=2\)</para><para id="para-00097">The correct answer is 2. \(\frac{1}{2}(-2)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 4=\frac{4}{2}=2\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="aebd7c88-b1e9-429d-8c26-0be943403732" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00026"><para id="para-00098">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00099"> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00026"><para id="para-00100">Correct! \(\frac{1}{2}(-1)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 1=\frac{1}{2}=0.5\)</para><para id="para-00101">The correct answer is 0.5. \(\frac{1}{2}(-1)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 1=\frac{1}{2}=0.5\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_19f7e9d6-11eb-42e9-8bc4-663b58043a4b" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00027"><para id="para-00102">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00103"> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00027"><para id="para-00104">Correct! \(\frac{1}{2}(0)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 0=0\)</para><para id="para-00105">The correct answer is 0. \(\frac{1}{2}(0)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 0=0\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_34793db7-7916-4c17-8e7d-5c350ef56e33" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00028"><para id="para-00106">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00107"> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00028"><para id="para-00108">Correct! \(\frac{1}{2}(1)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 1=\frac{1}{2}=0.5\)</para><para id="para-00109">The correct answer is 0.5. \(\frac{1}{2}(1)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 1=\frac{1}{2}=0.5\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a9602fee-e393-45f9-b26b-51f46f3fdc41" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00029"><para id="para-00110">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00111"> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00029"><para id="para-00112">Correct! \(\frac{1}{2}(2)2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 4=\frac{4}{2}=2\)</para><para id="para-00113">The correct answer is 2. \(\frac{1}{2}(2)2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 4=\frac{4}{2}=2\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="a99a5c26-6a0d-4e72-82ed-ec405c1f1e47" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00030"><para id="para-00114">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00115"> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(\frac{1}{2}x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00030"><para id="para-00116">Correct! \(\frac{1}{2}(3)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 9=\frac{9}{2}=4\frac{1}{2}=4.5\)</para><para id="para-00117">The correct answer is 4.5. \(\frac{1}{2}(3)^2=\frac{1}{2} \cdot 9=\frac{9}{2}=4\frac{1}{2}=4.5\)</para></solution></exercise></section>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated" id="list-00005">
  <item>Use the table with different values of \(x\) to answer questions a–g for the values of \(-2x^2\) . (You may
    also use a spreadsheet tool, if available.)</item>
</list>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00006">
  <tgroup cols="8"><tbody><row>
      <entry><emphasis> \(x\) </emphasis></entry><entry> -3 </entry>
      <entry> -2 </entry>
      <entry> -1 </entry>
      <entry> 0 </entry>
      <entry> 1 </entry>
      <entry> 2 </entry>
      <entry> 3 </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis> \(x^2\) </emphasis></entry><entry> 9 </entry>
      <entry> 4 </entry>
      <entry> 1 </entry>
      <entry> 0 </entry>
      <entry> 1 </entry>
      <entry> 4 </entry>
      <entry> 9 </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry><emphasis> \(-2x^2\) </emphasis></entry><entry> a. _____ </entry>
      <entry> b. _____ </entry>
      <entry> c. _____ </entry>
      <entry> d. _____ </entry>
      <entry> e. _____ </entry>
      <entry> f. _____ </entry>
      <entry> g. _____ </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody></tgroup></table>

<section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00006"><exercise id="_1ef18c42-7b66-4440-b804-f22f26238680" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00031"><para id="para-00118">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00119"> When \(x=-3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00031"><para id="para-00120">Correct! \(-2(-3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para><para id="para-00121">The correct answer is -18. \(-2(-3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_49a47e47-fe91-40f5-8b9c-f7e12aa93cb7" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00032"><para id="para-00122">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00123"> When \(x=-2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)?</para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00032"><para id="para-00124">Correct! \(-2(-2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para><para id="para-00125">The correct answer is -8. \(-2(-2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="de9fc74b-58ce-4763-bb13-43ffae05b658" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00033"><para id="para-00126">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00127"> When \(x=-1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00033"><para id="para-00128">Correct! \(-2(-1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para><para id="para-00129">The correct answer is -2. \(-2(-1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_6f548ba3-e63f-4dc7-85a0-e84b52b5bae7" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00034"><para id="para-00130">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00131"> When \(x=0\) and \(x^2=0\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00034"><para id="para-00132">Correct! \(-2(0)^2=-2 \cdot 0=0\)</para><para id="para-00133">The correct answer is 0. \(-2(0)^2=-2 \cdot 0=0\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_7cdbb75f-e4db-4503-9a20-d0cd22ce4d2f" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00035"><para id="para-00134">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00135"> When \(x=1\) and \(x^2=1\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00035"><para id="para-00136">Correct! \(-2(1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para><para id="para-00137">The correct answer is -2. \(-2(1)^2=-2 \cdot 1=-2\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_2bdcc76e-34cf-47ad-a401-e3883a0314a3" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00036"><para id="para-00138">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00139"> When \(x=2\) and \(x^2=4\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00036"><para id="para-00140">Correct! \(-2(2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para><para id="para-00141">The correct answer is -8. \(-2(2)^2=-2 \cdot 4=-8\)</para></solution></exercise><exercise id="_246cb693-cf66-408c-b773-b892056f5dcf" class="multiple-choice"><problem id="prob-00037"><para id="para-00142">Enter your answer here:</para><para id="para-00143"> When \(x=3\) and \(x^2=9\), what is value of \(-2x^2\)? </para>
      </problem><solution id="sol-00037"><para id="para-00144">Correct! \(-2(3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para><para id="para-00145">The correct answer is -18.\(-2(3)^2=-2 \cdot 9=-18\)</para></solution></exercise></section>
<example id="exam-00003"><exercise>
  <problem id="prob-00038"> 
